    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.67–0.70 from 7 h onward. The 18 h aliquot diluted 8-fold read 0.412 on average (0.4195 and 0.4043). Scaled back by 8, that is about 3.3 OD, roughly 5 times the undiluted 18 h reading of 0.673. If the reader were linear, the diluted and undiluted values would agree, so the reader is saturating at high density. The plateau therefore reflects the reader's ceiling, not stationary-phase biomass. The 3.3 estimate is a lower bound, because the diluted read at 0.41 may still be slightly compressed. I had no budget left to check other dilutions or time points."
